{"traj_id": "deepmath-52673_6", "problem": "Evaluate the integral: $$\\int_0^1 \\sqrt{\\frac{1-x^2}{x+2x^3+x^5}}\\,dx$$ using Euler's integral.", "gold": "\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}", "pred": "\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}", "is_correct": true, "tier": "medium", "n_tokens": 9561, "meta_leak": [], "paragraphs": ["We need to evaluate integral I = ∫_0^1 sqrt((1-x^2)/(x + 2x^3 + x^5)) dx.", "First simplify the denominator: x + 2x^3 + x^5 = x(1 + 2x^2 + x^4) = x(1+x^2)^2.", "So integrand becomes sqrt((1-x^2)/(x(1+x^2)^2)) = sqrt((1-x^2))/((1+x^2) sqrt(x)).", "So I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-x^2) / ((1+x^2) sqrt(x)) dx.", "Let's try substitution x = t^2, dx = 2t dt, sqrt(x) = t, x from 0 to 1 → t from 0 to 1.", "I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4) / ((1+t^4) t) · 2t dt = ∫_0^1 2 sqrt(1-t^4) / (1+t^4) dt.", "So I = 2 ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^4) dt.", "Now let's try another substitution. Let t^2 = tan θ? Or t = (something). Let me think about Euler's integral (Beta function).", "Euler's integral: B(p,q) = ∫_0^1 t^{p-1}(1-t)^{q-1} dt = 2∫_0^1 t^{p-1}(1-t^2)^{q-1} dt · something...", "Actually B(p,q) = 2∫_0^1 t^{2p-1}(1-t^2)^{q-1} dt.", "Let me try t^4 = sin^2 θ. Then t = sin^{1/2} θ, t^2 = sin θ, t^4 = sin^2 θ.\ndt = (1/2) sin^{-1/2} θ cos θ dθ.\nsqrt(1-t^4) = sqrt(1-sin^2 θ) = cos θ.\n1+t^4 = 1+sin^2 θ.", "I = 2 ∫_0^{π/2} cos θ / (1+sin^2 θ) · (1/2) sin^{-1/2} θ cos θ dθ\n= ∫_0^{π/2} sin^{-1/2} θ cos^2 θ / (1+sin^2 θ) dθ.", "Hmm, that's not immediately a Beta function. Let me try another approach.", "Let me try t^2 = u. Then I = 2 ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^4) dt. With t^2 = u, dt = du/(2√u):\nI = 2 ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-u^2)/(1+u^2) · du/(2√u) = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-u^2)/(√u (1+u^2)) du.", "Hmm, that's similar to what we had before. Let me go back to the original form.", "I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-x^2)/((1+x^2)√x) dx.", "Let me try x = sin θ. Then sqrt(1-x^2) = cos θ, dx = cos θ dθ, √x = √(sin θ), 1+x^2 = 1+sin^2 θ.", "I = ∫_0^{π/2} cos^2 θ / ((1+sin^2 θ) √(sin θ)) dθ.", "Hmm. Let me try x^2 = t. Then x = √t, dx = dt/(2√t):\nI = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t) / ((1+t) t) · dt/(2√t) ... wait let me redo.", "sqrt(1-x^2) = sqrt(1-t), (1+x^2) = (1+t), √x = t^{1/4}, dx = dt/(2√t).", "I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t) / ((1+t) t^{1/4}) · dt/(2√t) = (1/2) ∫_0^1 (1-t)^{1/2} / ((1+t) t^{3/4}) dt.", "That's a rational function times power. Let me try another substitution.", "Going back to I = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^4) dt.", "Let me try t = (1-u)/(1+u) or some rationalizing substitution.", "Actually, let me try t^2 = (1-u)/(1+u). Hmm, that might be complicated.", "Let me try t^2 = tan φ. Then t^4 = tan^2 φ, sqrt(1-t^4) = sqrt(1-tan^2 φ), 1+t^4 = 1+tan^2 φ = sec^2 φ. dt = (1/(2√(tan φ))) sec^2 φ dφ = sec^2 φ/(2√(tan φ)) dφ.", "I = 2∫_0^{π/4} sqrt(1-tan^2 φ) · sec^2 φ/(2√(tan φ)) · 1/sec^2 φ dφ\n= ∫_0^{π/4} sqrt(1-tan^2 φ)/√(tan φ) dφ.", "Hmm, that doesn't seem to simplify nicely either.\n\nLet me try another approach. Let's use the substitution t^2 = (1-u)/(1+u) in I = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^4) dt.", "Actually, let me reconsider. Let me try the substitution x = t/(1+t) or something.", "Wait, let me go back to I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-x^2)/((1+x^2)√x) dx.", "Let me try x^2 = t, so x = t^{1/2}, dx = (1/2)t^{-1/2} dt:\nI = ∫_0^1 (1-t)^{1/2} / ((1+t) t^{1/4}) · (1/2) t^{-1/2} dt\n= (1/2) ∫_0^1 (1-t)^{1/2} t^{-3/4} / (1+t) dt.", "Now use t = u/(1+u)? No, let's try the substitution 1+t = 1/(1-s)? Or t = (1-s)/(1+s)?", "Let me try t = (1-s)/(1+s). When t=0, s=1; when t=1, s=0.\ndt = -2/(1+s)^2 ds.\n1+t = 1 + (1-s)/(1+s) = 2/(1+s).\n1-t = 1 - (1-s)/(1+s) = 2s/(1+s).", "I = (1/2) ∫_1^0 (2s/(1+s))^{1/2} ((1-s)/(1+s))^{-3/4} / (2/(1+s)) · (-2/(1+s)^2) ds", "Let me compute step by step:\n(1-t)^{1/2} = (2s/(1+s))^{1/2} = √(2s)/√(1+s)\nt^{-3/4} = ((1-s)/(1+s))^{-3/4} = ((1+s)/(1-s))^{3/4}\n1/(1+t) = (1+s)/2\ndt = -2/(1+s)^2 ds", "Product: √(2s)/√(1+s) · ((1+s)/(1-s))^{3/4} · (1+s)/2 · (-2/(1+s)^2)", "= √(2s) · (1+s)^{-1/2} · (1+s)^{3/4} · (1-s)^{-3/4} · (1+s) · (-1/(1+s)^2)", "Wait, let me be more careful:\n= [√(2s) / (1+s)^{1/2}] · [(1+s)^{3/4} / (1-s)^{3/4}] · [(1+s)/2] · [-2/(1+s)^2] ds", "The constants: 1/2 · (-2) = -1\n(1+s) powers: -1/2 + 3/4 + 1 - 2 = -1/2 + 3/4 - 1 = -1/2 + 3/4 - 4/4 = -5/4 + 3/4 = -2/4 = -1/2", "Wait: -1/2 + 3/4 + 1 - 2 = (-2+3+4-8)/4 = (-3)/4 = -3/4", "So the (1+s) power is -3/4.\n\nSo the integrand becomes: -√(2s) · (1+s)^{-3/4} · (1-s)^{-3/4} ds", "= -√2 · s^{1/2} · [(1+s)(1-s)]^{-3/4} ds\n= -√2 · s^{1/2} · (1-s^2)^{-3/4} ds", "So I = (1/2) ∫_1^0 -√2 · s^{1/2} · (1-s^2)^{-3/4} ds = (1/2)√2 ∫_0^1 s^{1/2} (1-s^2)^{-3/4} ds.", "Now let s^2 = u, s = u^{1/2}, ds = (1/2)u^{-1/2} du:\ns^{1/2} = u^{1/4}\n(1-s^2)^{-3/4} = (1-u)^{-3/4}", "I = (1/2)√2 ∫_0^1 u^{1/4} (1-u)^{-3/4} · (1/2) u^{-1/2} du\n= (1/2)√2 · (1/2) ∫_0^1 u^{1/4 - 1/2} (1-u)^{-3/4} du\n= (√2/4) ∫_0^1 u^{-1/4} (1-u)^{-3/4} du\n= (√2/4) B(3/4, 1/4)", "where B(a,b) = ∫_0^1 t^{a-1}(1-t)^{b-1} dt.", "Here a-1 = -1/4, so a = 3/4. b-1 = -3/4, so b = 1/4.", "So I = (√2/4) B(3/4, 1/4) = (√2/4) · Γ(3/4)Γ(1/4)/Γ(1) = (√2/4) · Γ(3/4)Γ(1/4).", "Now use the reflection formula: Γ(z)Γ(1-z) = π/sin(πz).\nWith z = 1/4: Γ(1/4)Γ(3/4) = π/sin(π/4) = π/(√2/2) = 2π/√2 = π√2.", "So I = (√2/4) · π√2 = (√2 · π√2)/4 = (2π)/4 = π/2.", "So the integral equals π/2.\n\nLet me verify this numerically. The integrand at x = 0.5:\nsqrt((1-0.25)/(0.5 + 2·0.125 + 0.03125)) = sqrt(0.75/(0.5+0.25+0.03125)) = sqrt(0.75/0.78125) = sqrt(0.96) ≈ 0.9798.", "At x = 0.1: sqrt((1-0.01)/(0.1+0.002+0.00001)) = sqrt(0.99/0.10201) = sqrt(9.705) ≈ 3.115.", "At x = 0.9: sqrt((1-0.81)/(0.9+1.458+0.59049)) = sqrt(0.19/2.94849) = sqrt(0.06444) ≈ 0.2538.", "The function seems to be around 1-3 in the middle. The integral from 0 to 1 being π/2 ≈ 1.5708 seems reasonable.", "Actually wait, near x=0 the integrand behaves like sqrt(1/x) = 1/√x which is integrable. Near x=1 the integrand goes to 0. Let me check if π/2 makes sense.", "Let me do a rough numerical check. Using Simpson's rule with a few points:\nx=0: integrand → ∞ (like 1/√x)\nx=0.1: 3.115\nx=0.2: sqrt(0.96/(0.2+0.016+0.0032)) = sqrt(0.96/0.2192) = sqrt(4.379) ≈ 2.093\nx=0.3: sqrt(0.91/(0.3+0.054+0.00729)) = sqrt(0.91/0.36129) = sqrt(2.519) ≈ 1.587\nx=0.4: sqrt(0.84/(0.4+0.128+0.01024)) = sqrt(0.84/0.53824) = sqrt(1.561) ≈ 1.249\nx=0.5: 0.980\nx=0.6: sqrt(0.64/(0.6+0.432+0.07776)) = sqrt(0.64/1.10976) = sqrt(0.5767) ≈ 0.759\nx=0.7: sqrt(0.51/(0.7+0.686+0.16807)) = sqrt(0.51/1.55407) = sqrt(0.3282) ≈ 0.573", "x=0.8: sqrt(0.36/(0.8+1.024+0.32768)) = sqrt(0.36/2.15168) = sqrt(0.1673) ≈ 0.409\nx=0.9: 0.254\nx=1.0: 0", "This is tricky to integrate numerically due to the singularity at 0. But π/2 ≈ 1.5708 seems plausible.", "Let me double-check my algebra. Starting from:\nI = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-x^2)/((1+x^2)√x) dx.", "Sub x = t^2: I = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^4) dt. ✓", "Sub t^2 = u: dt = du/(2√u), t^4 = u^2.\nI = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-u^2)/(1+u^2) · du/(2√u) = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-u^2)/(√u(1+u^2)) du.", "Wait, I had I = (1/2)∫_0^1 (1-t)^{1/2}t^{-3/4}/(1+t) dt before. Let me recheck.", "From I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-x^2)/((1+x^2)√x) dx, substitute x = t^2:\nsqrt(1-x^2) = sqrt(1-t^4), (1+x^2) = (1+t^2), √x = t, dx = 2t dt.\nI = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/((1+t^2)t) · 2t dt = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^2) dt.", "Hmm wait, I wrote 1+t^4 earlier but it should be 1+t^2! Let me recheck.", "x + 2x^3 + x^5 = x(1 + 2x^2 + x^4) = x(1+x^2)^2. ✓", "So the integrand is sqrt((1-x^2)/(x(1+x^2)^2)) = sqrt(1-x^2)/((1+x^2)√x). ✓", "With x = t^2: 1+x^2 = 1+t^2, not 1+t^4. I made an error!", "Let me redo: I = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^2) dt.", "Now try t^2 = u: dt = du/(2√u).\nI = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-u^2)/(1+u) · du/(2√u) = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-u^2)/(√u(1+u)) du\n= ∫_0^1 u^{-1/2}(1-u)^{1/2}(1-u^{1/2})^{-1}(1+u^{1/2})^{-1} du.", "Hmm, that's messy. Let me try a different approach.\n\nActually, let me try the substitution directly on I = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^2) dt.", "Let t^2 = (1-u)/(1+u). Then t = sqrt((1-u)/(1+u)), t^2 = (1-u)/(1+u), t^4 = (1-u)^2/(1+u)^2.\n1-t^4 = 1-(1-u)^2/(1+u)^2 = [(1+u)^2-(1-u)^2]/(1+u)^2 = [1+2u+u^2-1+2u-u^2]/(1+u)^2 = 4u/(1+u)^2.\nsqrt(1-t^4) = 2√u/(1+u).\n1+t^2 = 1+(1-u)/(1+u) = 2/(1+u).", "dt: t = [(1-u)/(1+u)]^{1/2}\ndt/du = (1/2)[(1-u)/(1+u)]^{-1/2} · d/du[(1-u)/(1+u)]\nd/du[(1-u)/(1+u)] = [-(1+u)-(1-u)]/(1+u)^2 = -2/(1+u)^2.\nSo dt = (1/2)√((1+u)/(1-u)) · (-2/(1+u)^2) du = -√((1+u)/(1-u))/(1+u)^2 du = -1/[(1+u)^{3/2}√(1-u)] du.", "When t=0, u=1. When t=1, u=0.", "I = 2∫_1^0 [2√u/(1+u)] / [2/(1+u)] · [-1/((1+u)^{3/2}√(1-u))] du\n= 2∫_1^0 √u · [-1/((1+u)^{3/2}√(1-u))] du\n= -2∫_1^0 √u/[(1+u)^{3/2}√(1-u)] du\n= 2∫_0^1 √u/[(1+u)^{3/2}√(1-u)] du\n= 2∫_0^1 u^{1/2}(1-u)^{-1/2}(1+u)^{-3/2} du.", "Hmm, this is getting complicated. Let me try a different substitution.", "Actually, let me go back to I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-x^2)/((1+x^2)√x) dx and try x = sin θ.", "I = ∫_0^{π/2} cos θ/((1+sin^2 θ)√(sin θ)) · cos θ dθ = ∫_0^{π/2} cos^2 θ/((1+sin^2 θ)√(sin θ)) dθ.", "Hmm. Let me try another substitution. In I = 2∫_0^1 sqrt(1-t^4)/(1+t^2) dt, try t = tan^{1/2} φ or something.", "Actually, let me try t^2 = tan θ. Then t^4 = tan^2 θ, 1-t^4 = 1-tan^2 θ = (cos^2 θ - sin^2 θ)/cos^2 θ = cos 2θ/cos^2 θ. sqrt(1-t^4) = √(cos 2θ)/cos θ (for θ ∈ [0, π/4]).\n1+t^2 = 1+tan θ = (cos θ + sin θ)/cos θ.\ndt = (1/2)(tan θ)^{-1/2} sec^2 θ dθ = sec^2 θ/(2√(tan θ)) dθ.", "I = 2∫_0^{π/4} [√(cos 2θ)/cos θ] / [(cos θ+sin θ)/cos θ] · sec^2 θ/(2√(tan θ)) dθ\n= 2∫_0^{π/4} √(cos 2θ) / (cos θ+sin θ) · sec^2 θ/(2√(tan θ)) dθ\n= ∫_0^{π/4} √(cos 2θ) sec^2 θ/[(cos θ+sin θ)√(tan θ)] dθ.", "This is getting messy. Let me try yet another approach.\n\nGoing back to I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-x^2)/((1+x^2)√x) dx.", "Let me try the substitution x = (1-t)/(1+t). When x=0, t=1; when x=1, t=0.\ndx = -2/(1+t)^2 dt.\n1-x^2 = 1-(1-t)^2/(1+t)^2 = [(1+t)^2-(1-t)^2]/(1+t)^2 = 4t/(1+t)^2.\nsqrt(1-x^2) = 2√t/(1+t).\n1+x^2 = 1+(1-t)^2/(1+t)^2 = [(1+t)^2+(1-t)^2]/(1+t)^2 = [1+2t+t^2+1-2t+t^2]/(1+t)^2 = 2(1+t^2)/(1+t)^2.\n√x = √((1-t)/(1+t)).", "I = ∫_1^0 [2√t/(1+t)] / [2(1+t^2)/(1+t)^2 · √((1-t)/(1+t))] · [-2/(1+t)^2] dt", "Let me compute the integrand:\n= [2√t/(1+t)] · [(1+t)^2/(2(1+t^2))] · [√((1+t)/(1-t))] · [-2/(1+t)^2]", "= 2√t · (1+t)^2 · √(1+t) · (-2) / [(1+t) · 2(1+t^2) · √(1-t) · (1+t)^2]", "= -4√t · (1+t)^2 · (1+t)^{1/2} / [(1+t)^3 · (1+t^2) · (1-t)^{1/2}]", "Wait, let me redo this more carefully.\n\nNumerator factors: 2√t · (1+t)^2 · (1+t)^{1/2} · (-2)\nDenominator factors: (1+t) · 2(1+t^2) · (1-t)^{1/2} · (1+t)^2", "= 2√t · (1+t)^2 · (1+t)^{1/2} · (-2) / [(1+t) · 2(1+t^2) · (1-t)^{1/2} · (1+t)^2]", "Numerator: -4√t (1+t)^{2+1/2} = -4√t (1+t)^{5/2}\nDenominator: 2(1+t)^{1+2}(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2} = 2(1+t)^3(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2}", "= -4√t (1+t)^{5/2} / [2(1+t)^3(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2}]\n= -2√t (1+t)^{5/2-3} / [(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2}]\n= -2√t (1+t)^{-1/2} / [(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2}]\n= -2√(t/(1+t)) / [(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2}]\n= -2√t / [(1+t^2)√(1-t^2)]", "So I = ∫_1^0 -2√t/[(1+t^2)√(1-t^2)] dt = 2∫_0^1 √t/[(1+t^2)√(1-t^2)] dt.", "Now let t = sin φ. dt = cos φ dφ, √(1-t^2) = cos φ, √t = √(sin φ), 1+t^2 = 1+sin^2 φ.", "I = 2∫_0^{π/2} √(sin φ)/[(1+sin^2 φ) cos φ] · cos φ dφ\n= 2∫_0^{π/2} √(sin φ)/(1+sin^2 φ) dφ.", "Hmm, still not a standard Beta form.\n\nLet me try t = sin φ in 2∫_0^1 √t/[(1+t^2)√(1-t^2)] dt:\nI = 2∫_0^{π/2} √(sin φ)/(1+sin^2 φ) dφ.", "Let me try sin φ = u. Then cos φ dφ = du, dφ = du/cos φ = du/√(1-u^2).\nI = 2∫_0^1 √u/(1+u^2) · du/√(1-u^2) = 2∫_0^1 u^{1/2}/[(1+u^2)√(1-u^2)] du.", "Let u^2 = v. du = dv/(2√v), √u = v^{1/4}, √(1-u^2) = √(1-v), 1+u^2 = 1+v.\nI = 2∫_0^1 v^{1/4}/[(1+v)√(1-v)] · dv/(2√v) = ∫_0^1 v^{-1/4}/[(1+v)√(1-v)] dv\n= ∫_0^1 v^{-1/4}(1-v)^{-1/2}/(1+v) dv.", "Now use the substitution v = (1-w)/(1+w). When v=0, w=1; when v=1, w=0.\ndv = -2/(1+w)^2 dw.\n1+v = 1+(1-w)/(1+w) = 2/(1+w).\n1-v = 1-(1-w)/(1+w) = 2w/(1+w).", "I = ∫_1^0 [(1-w)/(1+w)]^{-1/4} [2w/(1+w)]^{-1/2} / [2/(1+w)] · [-2/(1+w)^2] dw", "= ∫_1^0 [(1+w)/(1-w)]^{1/4} · [√(1+w)/√(2w)] · [(1+w)/2] · [-2/(1+w)^2] dw", "Let me compute:\n(1+w)^{1/4} · (1-w)^{-1/4} · (1+w)^{1/2} · 2^{-1/2} · w^{-1/2} · (1+w)/2 · (-2/(1+w)^2)", "Powers of (1+w): 1/4 + 1/2 + 1 - 2 = 1/4 + 2/4 + 4/4 - 8/4 = -1/4\nPowers of (1-w): -1/4\nPowers of w: -1/2\nConstants: 2^{-1/2} · 1/2 · (-2) = -2^{-1/2} = -1/√2", "So integrand = -1/√2 · w^{-1/2} · (1-w)^{-1/4} · (1+w)^{-1/4}", "= -1/√2 · w^{-1/2} · [(1-w)(1+w)]^{-1/4}\n= -1/√2 · w^{-1/2} · (1-w^2)^{-1/4}", "I = ∫_1^0 -1/√2 · w^{-1/2} · (1-w^2)^{-1/4} dw = (1/√2)∫_0^1 w^{-1/2}(1-w^2)^{-1/4} dw.", "Now let w^2 = z. dw = dz/(2√z). w^{-1/2} = z^{-1/4}. (1-w^2)^{-1/4} = (1-z)^{-1/4}.", "I = (1/√2)∫_0^1 z^{-1/4}(1-z)^{-1/4} · dz/(2√z)\n= (1/(2√2))∫_0^1 z^{-1/4-1/2}(1-z)^{-1/4} dz\n= (1/(2√2))∫_0^1 z^{-3/4}(1-z)^{-1/4} dz\n= (1/(2√2))B(1/4, 3/4)", "where B(a,b) = Γ(a)Γ(b)/Γ(a+b), a = 1/4, b = 3/4.", "B(1/4, 3/4) = Γ(1/4)Γ(3/4)/Γ(1) = Γ(1/4)Γ(3/4) = π/sin(π/4) = π/(1/√2) = π√2.", "So I = (1/(2√2)) · π√2 = π/2.", "Great, so the answer is π/2.\n\nLet me verify the key steps once more.", "Original integral: I = ∫_0^1 sqrt((1-x^2)/(x+2x^3+x^5)) dx.", "x+2x^3+x^5 = x(1+x^2)^2. ✓", "I = ∫_0^1 sqrt(1-x^2)/[(1+x^2)√x] dx. ✓", "Sub x = (1-t)/(1+t), dx = -2/(1+t)^2 dt.\nx=0 → t=1, x=1 → t=0.", "1-x^2 = 1-(1-t)^2/(1+t)^2 = [(1+t)^2-(1-t)^2]/(1+t)^2 = 4t/(1+t)^2. ✓\nsqrt(1-x^2) = 2√t/(1+t). ✓\n1+x^2 = [(1+t)^2+(1-t)^2]/(1+t)^2 = 2(1+t^2)/(1+t)^2. ✓\n√x = √[(1-t)/(1+t)]. ✓", "Integrand × dx:\n[2√t/(1+t)] / [2(1+t^2)/(1+t)^2 · √((1-t)/(1+t))] · [-2/(1+t)^2] dt", "= [2√t/(1+t)] · [(1+t)^2/(2(1+t^2))] · [√((1+t)/(1-t))] · [-2/(1+t)^2] dt", "Let me multiply step by step:\n= 2√t · (1+t)^2 · (1+t)^{1/2} · (-2) / [(1+t) · 2(1+t^2) · (1-t)^{1/2} · (1+t)^2]", "Numerator: 2 · (-2) · √t · (1+t)^{2+1/2} = -4√t(1+t)^{5/2}\nDenominator: 2 · (1+t)^{1+2} · (1+t^2) · (1-t)^{1/2} = 2(1+t)^3(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2}", "= -4√t(1+t)^{5/2}/[2(1+t)^3(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2}]\n= -2√t(1+t)^{-1/2}/[(1+t^2)(1-t)^{1/2}]\n= -2√t/[(1+t^2)√((1+t)(1-t))]\n= -2√t/[(1+t^2)√(1-t^2)]", "So I = ∫_1^0 -2√t/[(1+t^2)√(1-t^2)] dt = 2∫_0^1 √t/[(1+t^2)√(1-t^2)] dt. ✓", "Now t = sin φ:\nI = 2∫_0^{π/2} √(sin φ)·cos φ/[(1+sin^2 φ)·cos φ] dφ = 2∫_0^{π/2} √(sin φ)/(1+sin^2 φ) dφ. ✓", "Now sin φ = u: dφ = du/√(1-u^2).\nI = 2∫_0^1 √u/[(1+u^2)√(1-u^2)] du. ✓", "Now u^2 = v: du = dv/(2√u) = dv/(2v^{1/2}).\n√u = v^{1/4}. √(1-u^2) = √(1-v). 1+u^2 = 1+v.", "I = 2∫_0^1 v^{1/4}/[(1+v)√(1-v)] · dv/(2v^{1/2})\n= ∫_0^1 v^{-1/4}/[(1+v)√(1-v)] dv. ✓", "Now v = (1-w)/(1+w): dv = -2/(1+w)^2 dw.\n1+v = 2/(1+w). 1-v = 2w/(1+w).", "I = ∫_1^0 [(1-w)/(1+w)]^{-1/4} · [2w/(1+w)]^{-1/2} · (1+w)/2 · [-2/(1+w)^2] dw", "= ∫_1^0 [(1+w)/(1-w)]^{1/4} · [(1+w)/(2w)]^{1/2} · [(1+w)/2] · [-2/(1+w)^2] dw", "Let me expand:\n= ∫_1^0 (1+w)^{1/4}(1-w)^{-1/4} · (1+w)^{1/2}·(2w)^{-1/2} · (1+w)/2 · (-2)/(1+w)^2 dw", "(1+w) powers: 1/4 + 1/2 + 1 - 2 = (1+2+4-8)/4 = -1/4 ✓\n(1-w) powers: -1/4 ✓\nw powers: -1/2 ✓\n2 powers: (2)^{-1/2} · 1/2 · (-2) = -2^{-1/2} · 2/2 = -2^{-1/2} = -1/√2 ✓", "So I = ∫_1^0 -1/√2 · w^{-1/2}(1-w)^{-1/4}(1+w)^{-1/4} dw\n= 1/√2 ∫_0^1 w^{-1/2}(1-w^2)^{-1/4} dw. ✓", "w^2 = z: dw = dz/(2w) = dz/(2√z). w^{-1/2} = z^{-1/4}.\nI = 1/√2 ∫_0^1 z^{-1/4}(1-z)^{-1/4} · dz/(2z^{1/2})\n= 1/(2√2) ∫_0^1 z^{-3/4}(1-z)^{-1/4} dz\n= 1/(2√2) B(1/4, 3/4)\n= 1/(2√2) · π√2\n= π/2. ✓\n\nSo the answer is π/2."], "answer_text": "# Evaluating the Integral via Euler's Integral (Beta Function)\n\n## Simplifying the Integrand\n\nFirst, factor the denominator:\n$$x + 2x^3 + x^5 = x(1 + 2x^2 + x^4) = x(1+x^2)^2$$\n\nSo the integral becomes:\n$$I = \\int_0^1 \\frac{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}{(1+x^2)\\sqrt{x}}\\,dx$$\n\n## Step 1: Substitution $x = \\frac{1-t}{1+t}$\n\nWith $dx = -\\frac{2}{(1+t)^2}dt$, the limits swap ($x=0\\to t=1$, $x=1\\to t=0$). Computing each piece:\n\n- $1-x^2 = \\frac{4t}{(1+t)^2} \\implies \\sqrt{1-x^2} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{t}}{1+t}$\n- $1+x^2 = \\frac{2(1+t^2)}{(1+t)^2}$\n- $\\sqrt{x} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1-t}{1+t}}$\n\nAfter multiplying and simplifying the powers of $(1+t)$:\n$$I = 2\\int_0^1 \\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{(1+t^2)\\sqrt{1-t^2}}\\,dt$$\n\n## Step 2: Substitution $t = \\sin\\varphi$, then $u = \\sin\\varphi$\n\n$$I = 2\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\sqrt{\\sin\\varphi}}{1+\\sin^2\\varphi}\\,d\\varphi = 2\\int_0^1 \\frac{u^{1/2}}{(1+u^2)\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\,du$$\n\n## Step 3: Substitution $u^2 = v$\n\n$$I = \\int_0^1 \\frac{v^{-1/4}}{(1+v)\\sqrt{1-v}}\\,dv$$\n\n## Step 4: Substitution $v = \\frac{1-w}{1+w}$\n\nComputing: $1+v = \\frac{2}{1+w}$, $\\;1-v = \\frac{2w}{1+w}$, $\\;dv = -\\frac{2}{(1+w)^2}dw$\n\nAfter carefully combining all factors:\n$$I = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int_0^1 w^{-1/2}(1-w^2)^{-1/4}\\,dw$$\n\n## Step 5: Substitution $w^2 = z$ (Euler's Beta Integral)\n\nWith $dw = \\frac{dz}{2\\sqrt{z}}$, $\\;w^{-1/2} = z^{-1/4}$:\n\n$$I = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\int_0^1 z^{-3/4}(1-z)^{-1/4}\\,dz = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\,B\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{3}{4}\\right)$$\n\n## Step 6: Evaluating the Beta Function\n\n$$B\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{3}{4}\\right) = \\frac{\\Gamma(1/4)\\,\\Gamma(3/4)}{\\Gamma(1)} = \\Gamma(1/4)\\,\\Gamma(3/4)$$\n\nApplying the **Euler reflection formula** $\\Gamma(z)\\,\\Gamma(1-z) = \\dfrac{\\pi}{\\sin(\\pi z)}$ with $z = \\tfrac{1}{4}$:\n\n$$\\Gamma(1/4)\\,\\Gamma(3/4) = \\frac{\\pi}{\\sin(\\pi/4)} = \\frac{\\pi}{1/\\sqrt{2}} = \\pi\\sqrt{2}$$\n\n## Final Result\n\n$$I = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\pi\\sqrt{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$$\n\n$$\\boxed{\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}}$$", "annotations": {"27B·v4": {"nodes": [{"node_id": 0, "p_start": 0, "p_end": 3, "label": "SU", "deps": [], "branch": 0, "path": "M", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 1, "p_start": 4, "p_end": 4, "label": "EX", "deps": [0], "branch": 1, "path": "D", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 2, "p_start": 5, "p_end": 6, "label": "CP", "deps": [1], "branch": 1, "path": "D", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 3, "p_start": 7, "p_end": 7, "label": "PL", "deps": [2], "branch": 1, "path": "D", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 4, "p_start": 8, "p_end": 9, "label": "RC", "deps": [3], "branch": 1, "path": "D", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 5, "p_start": 10, "p_end": 10, "label": "EX", "deps": [4], "branch": 2, "path": "D", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 6, "p_start": 11, "p_end": 11, "label": "CP", "deps": [5], "branch": 2, "path": "D", "flags": ""}, {